This project is a clean PHP reimplementation of the Turbo Vision text-mode
application framework. The PHP implementation is licensed under the MIT
License; see LICENSE.

Turbo Vision was created by Borland International. Borland released the
original Turbo Vision source code to the public while retaining its copyright.

The primary behavioral reference for this project is TVision 0.8, Sergio
Sigala's UNIX port of Turbo Vision 2.0. Sigala's changes are copyright (c) 1997
Sergio Sigala, Brescia, Italy, and are distributed under the BSD-style terms
preserved in docs/references/UPSTREAM-COPYRIGHT.txt.

The repository contains upstream C++ reference material and examples under
docs/references/ and examples/cpp/. Those files retain their original notices
and terms and are not covered by the MIT license for the PHP implementation.
